      "key": 1,
      "pattern": "pat-harness-over-model",
      "thesis": "The Harness Over the Model",
      "brief": "As multi-step and real-time agents move from demo to production, the load-bearing engineering shifts off the model and into the deterministic scaffolding around it — state machines, validators, turn-detection, rule engines, latency budgets. Reliability is reframed as a control problem, not a prompting problem; the frontier model is often the smallest, most swappable part of the system, and a smaller/faster/cheaper model plus scaffolding beats a bigger model driving itself.",
